From 4fd3b2e1bbc5fcca265ef0bd4470b97facd80ecd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christoph M. Becker" <cmbecker69@gmx.de>
Date: Tue, 23 Feb 2021 15:32:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/81] Fix #78719: http wrapper silently ignores long Location
 headers

When opening HTTP streams, and reading the headers, we currently
discard header lines longer than `HTTP_HEADER_BLOCK_SIZE` (1024 bytes).
While this is not generally forbidden by RFC 7230, section 3.2.5, it
is not generally allowed either, since that may change the "message
framing or response semantics".

We thus fix this by allowing arbitrarily long header lines.

Closes GH-6720.

(cherry picked from commit 51e2015af3fc4757a666736aae7899a43f76ae6d)
(cherry picked from commit 1c967cc72fea4202d573ab2afd3645ab46b4df15)
---
 ext/standard/http_fopen_wrapper.c     | 18 +++++-------------
 ext/standard/tests/http/bug78719.phpt | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 31 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 ext/standard/tests/http/bug78719.phpt

